    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d94">

                <pb facs="0231" n="132" xml:id="pg132"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.51244/48: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bullitt</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-12-14T15:00:00+00:00">December 14, 1936—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 14—11:10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1251. Department’s telegram No. 500, December 4, 7 p.m. Exchange of letters took
                    place today.</p>
                <p>Am I authorized to inform the French Government that on December 15, the date of
                    coming into effect of the agreement, it may use for the courts the information
                    already received by it from our customs authorities?<anchor n="84"
                        xml:id="d94-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bullitt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d94-f1" n="84" xml:id="d94-f1-content">
                <p>Authorization was granted in telegram No. 528, December 15, 1936, to the
                    Ambassador in France.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
